Planes?  My first ascension was in 3.0.j.  The endgame was one level. 
IIRC, the right third of the level was a maze, the middle third
consisted of 6 connected rooms, each containing one type of monster (a
room of trolls, a room of dragons, etc.).  After that, on the left
side was a bit more maze, and 3 attended high altars surrounded by
water.  No riders, no plane of air... but still rather hard.  There
were no potions of full healing, nor alchemy, nor artifacts other than
Excalibur, etc.  I'm not real sure, but I don't think there was dragon
scale mail, either.  If there was, I'm not sure gray dragons yet
existed, and I know there was no silver dragon scale mail (nor silver
dragons).

This was also back in the days that descending below the castle
dropped you into the first level of Gehennom, at which point you died
if you didn't have fire resistance.  Something like "You arrive in
hell without fire resistance.  You burn to a crisp!"

Ah, the good old days, when Rodney actually had a firm grip on his
amulet!

Anyway, I ascended this version a couple times before upgrading to
3.1.0.  I then ascended that several times before discovering that
tourists couldn't win that version (this was the first version with
the invocation, and the Master of Thieves didn't have the Bell of
Opening).  This was when I discovered rgrn with it's wealth of
spoilers (according to google, my FP was June 27, 1996)...

